{number: 89}
{title: All the Way My Saviour Leads Me}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] All the way my Savior leads me;
What have I to ask be-[Eb7] side?
Can I [Ab] doubt His tender [Db] mercy,
Who through [Ab] life has [Eb7] been my [Ab] Guide?
Heav'nly [Db] peace, divinest [Ab] comfort,
Here by [Eb7] faith in Him to [Ab] dwell!
For I [Db] know, whate'er be-[Ab] fall me,
Jesus [Eb7] doeth all things [Ab] well;
For I [Db] know, whate'er be-[Ab] fall me,
Jesus [Eb7] doeth all things [Ab] well.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] All the way my Savior leads me,
Cheers each winding path I [Eb7] tread,
Gives me [Ab] grace for every [Db] trial,
Feeds me [Ab] with the [Eb7] living [Ab] bread.
Though my [Db] weary steps may [Ab] falter,
And my [Eb7] soul athirst may [Ab] be,
Gushing [Db] from the Rock be-[Ab] fore me,
Lo! A [Eb7] spring of joy I [Ab] see;
Gushing [Db] from the Rock be-[Ab] fore me,
Lo! A [Eb7] spring of joy I [Ab] see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] All the way my Savior leads me,
Oh, the fullness of His [Eb7] love!
Perfect [Ab] rest to me is [Db] promised
In my [Ab] Father's [Eb7] house a-[Ab] bove.
When my [Db] spirit, clothed im-[Ab] mortal,
Wings its [Eb7] flight to realms of [Ab] day,
This my [Db] song through endless [Ab] ages:
Jesus [Eb7] led me all the [Ab] way;
This my [Db] song through endless [Ab] ages:
Jesus [Eb7] led me all the [Ab] way.
{end_of_verse}
